WEBVTT

00:00:00.594 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.719 --> 00:00:05.100
In this lesson I'll walk you through a complete gel polish set,

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.589
from the moment the client sits down to the final glossy top coat.

00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:10.573
Follow each step properly,

00:00:10.523 --> 00:00:14.270
and the nails will stay shiny and beautiful for two to three weeks.

00:00:14.937 --> 00:00:16.591
Please remember one thing for me:

00:00:16.999 --> 00:00:21.438
when gel polish lifts or chips, most of the time it's because of the nail prep,

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.271
not the bottle.

00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:24.751
That's why we'll take the prep really slowly.

00:00:25.342 --> 00:00:26.034
Step one:

00:00:26.474 --> 00:00:29.659
wash and sanitise your own hands and the client's hands,

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:33.074
then take a close look at the nails and the skin around them.

00:00:33.635 --> 00:00:39.558
If a nail is green or yellow, thickened or crumbly, or the skin is red, swollen,

00:00:39.508 --> 00:00:41.394
has pus or an open wound,

00:00:41.819 --> 00:00:44.834
don't do the service, and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:46.034
Also ask:

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.832
has the client ever had itching, red skin,

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.234
or nails coming loose after a gel service?

00:00:51.398 --> 00:00:55.154
If so, that may be a sign of an allergy, and you shouldn't go ahead.

00:00:55.753 --> 00:00:56.526
Step two:

00:00:56.766 --> 00:00:57.966
set out your tools.

00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:03.086
A cuticle pusher and cuticle nippers, sterilised and still sealed in their pouch.

00:01:03.497 --> 00:01:07.566
A 180 grit file and a fine buffer, a new set for every client.

00:01:07.994 --> 00:01:09.886
Lint-free wipes and nail cleanser.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.606
Base gel, colour gel and top gel.

00:01:12.955 --> 00:01:13.646
An LED

00:01:13.596 --> 00:01:16.206
lamp, wooden sticks, and cuticle oil.

00:01:16.478 --> 00:01:19.246
And wear gloves, to protect the skin on your own hands.

00:01:19.881 --> 00:01:20.695
Step three:

00:01:21.023 --> 00:01:21.975
shape the nails.

00:01:22.295 --> 00:01:26.824
Hold the file at a slight angle under the free edge, and file in one direction,

00:01:26.774 --> 00:01:28.695
from the side towards the centre.

00:01:29.025 --> 00:01:30.383
Don't saw back and forth,

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:33.575
because the nail heats up and can start to split into layers.

00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:37.175
Do all ten nails evenly, in the shape the client has chosen.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:38.621
Step four:

00:01:38.851 --> 00:01:39.661
the cuticle.

00:01:40.057 --> 00:01:44.477
We work dry, with no soaking, because a nail that soaks up water swells,

00:01:44.427 --> 00:01:46.541
then shrinks back after polishing,

00:01:46.807 --> 00:01:48.141
and the gel lifts easily.

00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:50.797
Hold the pusher at about 45 degrees,

00:01:50.747 --> 00:01:53.981
and gently push the skin at the base of the nail back.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:58.861
Then scrape off the thin, clear layer of skin still stuck to the nail plate.

00:01:59.209 --> 00:02:02.621
That thin layer is exactly what makes gel lift at the cuticle.

00:02:03.235 --> 00:02:08.230
With the nippers, cut only the dead skin that has lifted, the white, dry part.

00:02:08.648 --> 00:02:10.230
Never cut into living skin.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.230
Cutting too deep makes it bleed, and opens the way to infection.

00:02:14.935 --> 00:02:15.834
Step five:

00:02:16.078 --> 00:02:16.634
buffing.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:20.595
Glide the fine buffer very lightly over the whole nail plate,

00:02:20.545 --> 00:02:22.074
just to take the shine off.

00:02:22.582 --> 00:02:26.915
Pay attention to the area right next to the cuticle and along both sides of the nail,

00:02:26.865 --> 00:02:28.074
which are easy to miss.

00:02:28.582 --> 00:02:29.434
Don't buff hard:

00:02:29.703 --> 00:02:32.154
a thinner nail is weaker, and it hurts.

00:02:32.793 --> 00:02:33.680
Step six:

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:34.480
cleansing.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:39.061
Brush off all the dust, then take a lint-free wipe with nail cleanser,

00:02:39.011 --> 00:02:40.799
and wipe each nail thoroughly,

00:02:40.886 --> 00:02:43.280
including both sides and the free edge.

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:45.859
From now on, don't touch the nail plate,

00:02:45.809 --> 00:02:48.132
and remind the client not to touch it either,

00:02:48.082 --> 00:02:50.960
because the oil on the skin stops the gel from sticking.

00:02:51.387 --> 00:02:55.079
If your gel brand also has a bonder or primer, apply it now,

00:02:55.029 --> 00:02:56.960
exactly as the brand instructs.

00:02:57.607 --> 00:02:58.396
Step seven:

00:02:58.727 --> 00:02:59.436
the base coat.

00:03:00.164 --> 00:03:02.156
Take very little gel on the brush.

00:03:02.472 --> 00:03:06.474
Place the brush in the middle of the nail, a little away from the cuticle,

00:03:06.424 --> 00:03:08.396
gently push it up close to the skin,

00:03:08.743 --> 00:03:13.116
leaving a gap as thin as a hair, then pull straight down to the free edge.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.556
Then do the sides.

00:03:14.737 --> 00:03:18.476
Finally, run the brush across the tip of the free edge to cap it.

00:03:18.985 --> 00:03:21.436
The base coat must be really thin and even.

00:03:22.078 --> 00:03:23.199
The golden rule:

00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:25.199
gel must never touch the skin.

00:03:25.862 --> 00:03:30.453
Gel on the skin makes the polish lift, and it can also cause an allergy later on,

00:03:30.403 --> 00:03:32.639
for both the client and the technician.

00:03:33.305 --> 00:03:34.815
If some does get on the skin,

00:03:34.765 --> 00:03:38.239
wipe it away with a wooden stick before the hand goes into the lamp.

00:03:38.855 --> 00:03:40.642
Now the hand goes into the lamp.

00:03:40.971 --> 00:03:41.842
With an LED

00:03:41.792 --> 00:03:44.402
lamp, it's usually thirty to sixty seconds.

00:03:44.672 --> 00:03:45.362
With a UV

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.042
lamp, about two minutes.

00:03:47.551 --> 00:03:51.479
Every brand is different, so always follow the time given on the product,

00:03:51.429 --> 00:03:54.082
and use the type of lamp your gel brand requires.

00:03:54.587 --> 00:03:56.722
Under-cured gel is not fully hardened:

00:03:56.991 --> 00:04:00.082
it lifts easily, and it's more likely to cause an allergy.

00:04:00.676 --> 00:04:01.686
An important tip:

00:04:02.035 --> 00:04:05.926
paint and cure four fingers first, and do the thumbs on their own.

00:04:06.357 --> 00:04:08.486
The thumb has to lie flat in the lamp.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.446
If it's tilted, the gel runs to one side.

00:04:12.025 --> 00:04:12.817
Step eight:

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.257
the first colour coat.

00:04:14.506 --> 00:04:16.017
Same principle as before:

00:04:16.126 --> 00:04:16.657
thin.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.097
Three brush strokes:

00:04:18.206 --> 00:04:21.137
one down the middle, one on the left, one on the right.

00:04:21.566 --> 00:04:23.537
Cap the free edge, then cure.

00:04:23.784 --> 00:04:26.716
Don't worry if the first coat looks patchy, that's normal,

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.257
so don't try to paint it thick.

00:04:28.606 --> 00:04:31.537
A thick coat wrinkles, and doesn't cure all the way through.

00:04:32.222 --> 00:04:35.149
The second colour coat is done exactly the same way:

00:04:35.415 --> 00:04:39.069
thin, three strokes, cap the free edge, cure.

00:04:39.578 --> 00:04:41.709
Now the colour is even and beautiful.

00:04:41.976 --> 00:04:46.269
With very dark or very light shades, you may need a thin third coat.

00:04:46.946 --> 00:04:47.808
Step nine:

00:04:48.061 --> 00:04:48.848
the top coat.

00:04:49.168 --> 00:04:52.608
Cover all of the colour, the free edge included, to seal it in.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.129
The top coat can be a little thicker than the colour coats, for a smooth,

00:04:57.079 --> 00:04:57.888
glassy finish.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:02.048
Cure it for the full time, usually sixty seconds in an LED

00:05:02.078 --> 00:05:02.448
lamp.

00:05:03.141 --> 00:05:06.936
If your top coat leaves a sticky layer, then after curing,

00:05:06.886 --> 00:05:09.584
take a lint-free wipe with nail cleanser,

00:05:09.774 --> 00:05:11.904
and wipe the sticky layer off the surface.

00:05:12.327 --> 00:05:14.864
If it's a no-wipe top coat, skip this step.

00:05:15.498 --> 00:05:16.318
Last step:

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:21.358
put a drop of cuticle oil on the skin around each nail, and massage it in gently.

00:05:21.773 --> 00:05:25.998
Soft skin, shiny nails, and the client loves them straight away.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:28.812
Give the client three pieces of advice.

00:05:28.981 --> 00:05:29.532
One:

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.852
wear gloves when washing up or cleaning.

00:05:32.182 --> 00:05:32.732
Two:

00:05:32.923 --> 00:05:34.812
use cuticle oil every day.

00:05:35.076 --> 00:05:35.692
Three:

00:05:36.027 --> 00:05:39.830
don't pick the gel off, but come back to the salon in two to three weeks,

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.372
to have it removed and redone.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:44.578
The client has gone, but the job isn't finished:

00:05:44.822 --> 00:05:48.738
metal tools go to be washed, disinfected and sterilised.

00:05:49.165 --> 00:05:50.978
Single-use items go in the bin.

00:05:51.326 --> 00:05:53.058
Wipe down the table and the lamp.

00:05:53.565 --> 00:05:57.858
And now, take the short quiz below the video, and see how much you remember.
